  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kakeya Toranpu (Etori). Type: Partnership trick-taking. Deck: 52 cards. Hand: 13 cards. Special: Rensho (Ace of Spades) wins any trick. Scoring: Only J-Q-K-A count (16 total). Win 9-11 = 1 stone, 12-15 = 2 stones, 16 = 4 stones. Game ends when team loses all 5 stones.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Kakeya Toranpu, a rare Japanese treasure! Your goal is to capture face cards (J-Q-K-A). Save your Rensho (Ace of Spades) for the perfect momentâ€”it wins any trick! Can you capture 9+ face cards to win Go stones?',
    objective: "Win 'Face Cards' (J-Q-K-A) in tricks. The team that captures 9 or more of the 16 face cards wins a Go stone from their opponents.",
    gameplay: '1. Players draw lottery sticks to determine partnerships.\n2. Trump (Kiri) is determined by a cut or rotation.\n3. Must follow suit if possible; if not, any card can be played.\n4. **Scoring**: Only Face cards (16 total) matter. Winning 9-11 = 1 stone, 12-15 = 2 stones, 16 (All) = 4 stones.',
    keyRules: [
      'The Rensho (usually Ace of Spades) is the highest card and wins any trick it is played to',
      'Players draw lottery sticks to determine partnerships',
      'Trump is determined by cut or rotation',
      'Must follow suit if possible',
      'Only Jacks, Queens, Kings, and Aces (16 total) count for scoring',
      'Game ends when a team loses all 5 starting Go stones',
    ],
